  "configuration_id": "config_023",
  "reason": "Evidence: All five completed experiments use singleprofile; the multiprofile dimension is entirely unexplored. The best configuration so far is config_032 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) at 0.536 acc, showing that scvi_n200 slightly outperforms pca_n2000 and concat slightly outperforms weighted fusion. Question: Does extending the best-known single-profile setup to multiprofile with transformer aggregation yield a meaningful gain, or does the added complexity fail to help? This directly tests whether multiple profiles carry complementary information that a transformer can exploit. Why best next experiment: The profile setting is the largest unexplored design axis and could have a larger impact than swapping the image encoder (which contributes only ~4% over RNA alone). Config_023 extends config_032 minimally—keeping the proven scvi_n200 encoder, resnet50 image encoder, and concat fusion—while introducing multiprofile with the most expressive aggregation (transformer). If it succeeds, it opens a productive direction; if it fails, we learn that multiprofile does not help under current settings and can redirect budget toward image-encoder or RNA-encoder variants. This is the highest-information experiment available under the constraint that multiprofile necessarily requires an aggregation choice."
}

